--   These are obtained by showing that every six-element index set in the relevant ranges has $z_I=0$, using the genus-1 quotients and the five-square method. They extend the verified range of the strong conjecture beyond the elementary base cases.
-- source:
--   E. González-Jiménez and X. Xarles, 'On a conjecture of Rudin on squares in arithmetic progressions', LMS J. Comput. Math. 17(1) (2014) 58–76, doi:10.1112/S1461157013000259, §6, p. 73.

